From 12ff951298eb25e30252d92e999697ba9f48a921 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:33:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] input: add touchpad gesture bindings

Multi-finger touchpad swipes and pinches were only ever passed on to the
client, so the compositor could not be driven with them.

A new <touchpad> section of rc.xml binds them to actions:

  <touchpad>
    <gesture type="swipe" fingers="3" direction="left">
      <action name="GoToDesktop" to="right" />
    </gesture>
  </touchpad>

type is swipe or pinch, fingers is 3 to 5 for a swipe and 2 to 5 for a
pinch, direction is left, right, up or down for a swipe (the way the
fingers move) and in or out for a pinch. All three are required and an
entry with a bad value is dropped with an error.

A gesture is claimed when it begins if anything is bound for its type
and number of fingers, and stays claimed until it ends, so the client
sees either all of a gesture or none of it, also across a Reconfigure.
The actions run once per gesture: for a swipe when the fingers have
travelled 100 units along the longer axis, for a pinch when they are at
0.8 or 1.25 times their first spread. The last definition of a gesture
wins. Nothing is claimed or run while the session is locked. Gestures
with no binding for their type and finger count are passed on as before.

t/gesture.c covers the names and thresholds, t/gesture-handlers.c drives
the handlers with touchpad events around a stubbed compositor.
